{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"An $\\blueE{\\text{exponent}}$ tells us how many factors of a $\\maroonD{\\text{base}}$ we should multiply to find the value of an expression.\n\nWe write exponential expressions like this: $\\maroonD{\\text{base}}^\\blueE{\\text{exponent}}$\n\nFor example,\n\n$\\maroonD{5}^\\blueE{3}=\\maroonD{5} \\times \\maroonD{5} \\times \\maroonD{5}$\n\nLet's use this definition to decide if each equation is true or false.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$2^4 = 2 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\times 2$ \n\nSo,  $2^4=2\\times4$ is false.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$2^4 = 2 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\times 2$ \n\nSo,  $2^4=4+4$ is false.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"By definition, $2^4 = 2 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\times 2$ is true.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"[[☃ categorizer 4]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"categorizer 4":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"categories":["True","False"],"items":["$2^4=2 \\times 4$","$2^4=4+4$","$2^4=2 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\times 2$"],"linterContext":{"contentType":"","highlightLint":false,"paths":[],"stack":[]},"randomizeItems":false,"static":false,"values":[1,1,0]},"static":true,"type":"categorizer","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Determine whether each equation is true or false.**\n\n[[☃ categorizer 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"categorizer 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"categories":["True","False"],"items":["$2^4=2 \\times 4$","$2^4=4+4$","$2^4=2 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\times 2$"],"linterContext":{"contentType":"","highlightLint":false,"paths":[],"stack":[]},"randomizeItems":false,"static":false,"values":[1,1,0]},"static":false,"type":"categorizer","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}}}
